### SecurityHub — coleção de requisições
### Compatível com o REST Client do VS Code e com o cliente HTTP do IntelliJ.
### Nenhum segredo aqui: o token é capturado da resposta de login em tempo de execução.
###
### O arquivo é um fluxo: executado de cima para baixo contra uma pilha com o perfil `demo`
### (docker compose up), cada bloco alimenta o seguinte através das variáveis capturadas.
### A seção 11 reúne os casos negativos e a 12 desfaz o que foi criado.
### Resposta detalhada de cada endpoint: docs/api-examples.md

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1
@demoEmail = admin@demo.test
@demoPassword = Demo@SecurityHub2026

############################################################
### 1. Autenticação
############################################################

### 1.1 Cadastro de uma nova empresa com o primeiro administrador
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyName": "Acme Segurança",
  "name": "Administrador",
  "email": "admin@acme.test",
  "password": "uma-senha-suficientemente-longa"
}

### 1.2 Login — guarda o access token para as chamadas seguintes
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{demoEmail}}",
  "password": "{{demoPassword}}"
}

@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
@userId = {{login.response.body.user.id}}

### 1.3 Usuário autenticado
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 1.4 Login como DEVELOPER — usado nos casos de 403 da seção 11
# @name loginDeveloper
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "developer@demo.test",
  "password": "{{demoPassword}}"
}

@devToken = {{loginDeveloper.response.body.accessToken}}

### 1.5 Login como VIEWER — papel estritamente somente leitura
# @name loginViewer
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "viewer@demo.test",
  "password": "{{demoPassword}}"
}

@viewerToken = {{loginViewer.response.body.accessToken}}

### 1.6 Login no segundo tenant — usado nos casos de 404 por isolamento
# @name loginOtherCompany
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@northwind.test",
  "password": "{{demoPassword}}"
}

@otherToken = {{loginOtherCompany.response.body.accessToken}}

############################################################
### 2. Projetos
############################################################

### 2.1 Listagem paginada, filtrada e ordenada
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects?page=0&size=20&sort=createdAt,desc&search=portal&status=ACTIVE
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.2 Criar projeto (somente ADMIN)
# @name createProject
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Portal do Cliente",
  "description": "Aplicação web voltada ao cliente final",
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

@projectId = {{createProject.response.body.id}}

### 2.3 Detalhe do projeto
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.4 Atualizar projeto
PUT {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Portal do Cliente",
  "description": "Descrição revisada",
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

############################################################
### 3. Ativos
############################################################

### 3.1 Listagem com todos os filtros do módulo
GET {{baseUrl}}/assets?page=0&size=20&sort=criticality,desc&search=api&projectId={{projectId}}&type=API&environment=PRODUCTION&criticality=CRITICAL
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3.2 Criar ativo (somente ADMIN)
# @name createAsset
POST {{baseUrl}}/assets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "projectId": {{projectId}},
  "name": "API de pagamentos",
  "description": "Processa cobranças e estornos",
  "type": "API",
  "identifier": "api.pagamentos.acme.test",
  "environment": "PRODUCTION",
  "criticality": "CRITICAL"
}

@assetId = {{createAsset.response.body.id}}

### 3.3 Detalhe do ativo
GET {{baseUrl}}/assets/{{assetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3.4 Atualizar ativo — identifier em branco significa "sem identificador"
PUT {{baseUrl}}/assets/{{assetId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "projectId": {{projectId}},
  "name": "API de pagamentos",
  "description": "Processa cobranças, estornos e conciliação",
  "type": "API",
  "identifier": "api.pagamentos.acme.test",
  "environment": "PRODUCTION",
  "criticality": "HIGH"
}

############################################################
### 4. Vulnerabilidades
############################################################

### 4.1 Listagem com todos os filtros do módulo
GET {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities?page=0&size=20&sort=cvssScore,desc&search=injection&projectId={{projectId}}&assetId={{assetId}}&severity=CRITICAL&status=OPEN&overdue=false
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.2 Criar vulnerabilidade (ADMIN ou ANALYST) — nasce sempre OPEN, sem status no corpo
# @name createVulnerability
POST {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "assetId": {{assetId}},
  "title": "SQL injection no endpoint de busca",
  "description": "Parâmetro concatenado diretamente na query",
  "severity": "CRITICAL",
  "cvssScore": 9.1,
  "cve": "CVE-2024-12345",
  "discoveredAt": "2026-09-17T12:02:00Z",
  "dueDate": "2026-10-01T00:00:00Z"
}

@vulnerabilityId = {{createVulnerability.response.body.id}}

### 4.3 Detalhe da vulnerabilidade
GET {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities/{{vulnerabilityId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.4 Atribuir a um usuário ativo da própria empresa (ADMIN ou ANALYST)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities/{{vulnerabilityId}}/assignee
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "userId": {{userId}}
}

### 4.5 Alterar status para IN_PROGRESS
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities/{{vulnerabilityId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "status": "IN_PROGRESS"
}

### 4.6 Atualizar a vulnerabilidade — PUT nunca altera status nem resolvedAt
PUT {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities/{{vulnerabilityId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "assetId": {{assetId}},
  "title": "SQL injection no endpoint de busca de pedidos",
  "description": "Parâmetro concatenado diretamente na query; reproduzido em homologação",
  "severity": "CRITICAL",
  "cvssScore": 9.4,
  "cve": "CVE-2024-12345",
  "discoveredAt": "2026-09-17T12:02:00Z",
  "dueDate": "2026-10-01T00:00:00Z",
  "assignedToId": {{userId}}
}

### 4.7 Itens atrasados — overdue=true usa o mesmo predicado do card do dashboard
GET {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities?overdue=true&sort=dueDate,asc&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.8 Painel "itens recentes" do dashboard — é esta listagem, não um quinto endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities?page=0&size=5&sort=createdAt,desc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

############################################################
### 5. Comentários
############################################################

### 5.1 Comentar (ADMIN, ANALYST ou DEVELOPER)
# @name createComment
POST {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities/{{vulnerabilityId}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "content": "Correção iniciada; o parâmetro passa a usar bind."
}

@commentId = {{createComment.response.body.id}}

### 5.2 Listar comentários — ordem ascendente por createdAt, ao contrário do resto da API
GET {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities/{{vulnerabilityId}}/comments?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5.3 Editar o próprio comentário (autor ou ADMIN)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities/{{vulnerabilityId}}/comments/{{commentId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "content": "Correção iniciada; o parâmetro passa a usar bind. PR aberto."
}

############################################################
### 6. Resolver
############################################################

### 6.1 Entrar em RESOLVED carimba resolvedAt; sair de RESOLVED limparia o carimbo
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities/{{vulnerabilityId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "status": "RESOLVED"
}

### 6.2 Desatribuir — userId nulo é uma requisição válida
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities/{{vulnerabilityId}}/assignee
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "userId": null
}

############################################################
### 7. Usuários
############################################################

### 7.1 Usuários da empresa (ADMIN e ANALYST) — array puro, sem paginação
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?active=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7.2 Filtrado por papel e texto
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?role=DEVELOPER&active=true&search=mendes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

############################################################
### 8. Auditoria
############################################################

### 8.1 Trilha de auditoria (somente ADMIN)
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs?page=0&size=20&entityType=Project
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8.2 Filtrada por ação, ator e janela de tempo
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs?page=0&size=50&entityType=Vulnerability&action=STATUS_CHANGE&actorId={{userId}}&from=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-12-31T23:59:59Z&sort=createdAt,desc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

############################################################
### 9. Dashboard
############################################################

### 9.1 Cards — openVulnerabilities é OPEN + IN_PROGRESS, não uma contagem de status
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9.2 Distribuição por severidade — array com as quatro severidades, inclusive as zeradas
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard/severity-distribution
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9.3 Distribuição por status — array com os quatro status, inclusive os zerados
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard/status-distribution
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9.4 Série diária de abertas e resolvidas
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard/trend?days=30
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9.5 days é limitado em silêncio a [1, 90] — responde 200 com "days": 90
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard/trend?days=365
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

############################################################
### 10. Comportamentos silenciosos que vale ver
############################################################

### 10.1 sort fora da allowlist é descartado — confira "sort" na resposta: "createdAt,desc"
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects?sort=passwordHash,asc&size=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10.2 size acima do máximo é limitado a 100 — confira "size" na resposta
GET {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities?size=500
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

############################################################
### 11. Casos negativos
############################################################

### 11.1 Endpoint protegido sem token — esperado 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects

### 11.2 Token inválido — esperado 401 UNAUTHORIZED (mesmo corpo do caso anterior)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer token-invalido-qualquer

### 11.3 Credenciais erradas — esperado 401 com "Credenciais inválidas"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{demoEmail}}",
  "password": "senha-obviamente-errada"
}

### 11.4 DEVELOPER criando projeto — esperado 403 FORBIDDEN ("Acesso negado")
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{devToken}}

{
  "name": "Projeto que o developer não pode criar"
}

### 11.5 DEVELOPER alterando status de item atribuído a outra pessoa
### Esperado 403 com "Você só pode alterar o status de vulnerabilidades atribuídas a você"
### (execute 4.4 antes: o item precisa estar atribuído ao ADMIN)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities/{{vulnerabilityId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{devToken}}

{
  "status": "RESOLVED"
}

### 11.6 VIEWER comentando — esperado 403 FORBIDDEN, o papel é somente leitura
POST {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities/{{vulnerabilityId}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{viewerToken}}

{
  "content": "Comentário que o viewer não pode escrever"
}

### 11.7 DEVELOPER consultando auditoria — esperado 403 FORBIDDEN (só ADMIN)
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{devToken}}

### 11.8 Projeto de outra empresa — esperado 404 NOT_FOUND, nunca 403
### Um 403 confirmaria que a linha existe e transformaria a API em um oráculo de enumeração
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{otherToken}}

### 11.9 Excluir recurso de outra empresa — esperado 404 NOT_FOUND
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities/{{vulnerabilityId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{otherToken}}

### 11.10 Referência a um projeto inexistente no corpo — esperado 404 ("Projeto ... não encontrado")
POST {{baseUrl}}/assets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "projectId": 999999,
  "name": "Ativo órfão",
  "type": "SERVER",
  "environment": "TEST",
  "criticality": "LOW"
}

### 11.11 Responsável desconhecido, inativo ou de outra empresa — esperado 404 ("Usuário ... não encontrado")
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities/{{vulnerabilityId}}/assignee
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "userId": 999999
}

### 11.12 Nome de projeto duplicado — esperado 409 CONFLICT
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Portal do Cliente"
}

### 11.13 Identificador de ativo duplicado no mesmo projeto — esperado 409 CONFLICT
POST {{baseUrl}}/assets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "projectId": {{projectId}},
  "name": "Outro ativo, mesmo identificador",
  "type": "API",
  "identifier": "api.pagamentos.acme.test",
  "environment": "PRODUCTION",
  "criticality": "LOW"
}

### 11.14 E-mail já cadastrado — esperado 409 CONFLICT (unicidade é global, não por empresa)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyName": "Outra Empresa",
  "name": "Outro Administrador",
  "email": "{{demoEmail}}",
  "password": "uma-senha-suficientemente-longa"
}

### 11.15 Excluir projeto que ainda tem ativos — esperado 409 CONFLICT com a contagem
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11.16 Excluir ativo que ainda tem vulnerabilidades — esperado 409 CONFLICT com a contagem
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/assets/{{assetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11.17 Payload inválido — esperado 400 VALIDATION_ERROR com fieldErrors
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": ""
}

### 11.18 Vários campos inválidos de uma vez — esperado 400 com quatro fieldErrors
POST {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "ab",
  "cvssScore": 12.5
}

### 11.19 Valor de enum inexistente — esperado 400 BAD_REQUEST, sem fieldErrors
### A falha é de desserialização e acontece antes da validação rodar
POST {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "assetId": {{assetId}},
  "title": "Severidade que não existe",
  "severity": "URGENTE"
}

### 11.20 Tipo incompatível na query — esperado 400 BAD_REQUEST
GET {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities?projectId=abc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

############################################################
### 12. Limpeza — na ordem que respeita a regra de filhos
############################################################

### 12.1 Excluir a vulnerabilidade (somente ADMIN); os comentários vão junto
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/vulnerabilities/{{vulnerabilityId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12.2 Excluir o ativo, agora sem filhos
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/assets/{{assetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12.3 Excluir o projeto, agora sem filhos
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
